          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-13 17:20:39.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20315 ptlrpc: mark module init functions __init",
        "message": "LU-20315 ptlrpc: mark module init functions __init\n\nThe helpers that ptlrpc_init() calls once at module load, and the\nhelpers they call in turn, are only reachable during initialisation:\nrequest cache and XID setup, connection table, LNet portals, lproc\nand sysfs registration, NRS, the pinger, the HR threads, sptlrpc and\nits null, plain and gss flavours, nodemap, early reply size and the\nwire constant assertions.\n\nMark them __init so the kernel places them in the init section and\nfrees them once ptlrpc_init() returns, instead of keeping them\nresident for the life of the module.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5e37805c5b11489b92cadc360a842ab36a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
